பசி","lemma":"paci","gloss":"hunger"}],"gloss":"hunger"},{"surface":"போக்கல்","parts":[{"text":"போக்கு","lemma":"pōkku","gloss":"remove"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"al","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"removing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அண்ணல்","parts":[{"text":"அண்ணல்","lemma":"aṇṇal","gloss":"noble lord"}],"gloss":"noble"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"yāṉai","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"வேந்தர்","parts":[{"text":"வேந்தர்","lemma":"vēntar","gloss":"kings"}],"gloss":"kings"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உண்மையோ","parts":[{"text":"உண்மை","lemma":"uṇmai","gloss":"existence"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"interrogative/emphasis"}],"gloss":"existence"},{"surface":"அறியலர்","parts":[{"text":"அறி","lemma":"aṟi","gloss":"know"},{"text":"அலர்","lemma":"alar","gloss":"not they"}],"gloss":"they do not know"},{"surface":"காண்பு","parts":[{"text":"காண்","lemma":"kāṇ","gloss":"see"},{"text":"பு","lemma":"pu","gloss":"noun suffix"}],"gloss":"seeing"},{"surface":"அறியலரே","parts":[{"text":"அறி","lemma":"aṟi","gloss":"know"},{"text":"அலர்","lemma":"alar","gloss":"not they"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"they have never known"}]}],"literal":"Like cowherds with righteous hearts growing up / like motherless children with cruel hearts / where rare-flowered cerunti blooms in the tall forest, fragrant / like a wide festival-adorned ground, in the courtyard / if friends approach, except guards / even without permission do not approach, the protected wide mansion / like a group of mountains, the mansion resounded, my / ringing-voiced taṭāri drum to resound loudly, having beaten / having sung and stood for many days, not only / on the past day, having gone in the anxious night / for coming, taking, at the tall gate stood / the sparse-haired bard is pitiable himself, saying / to approach near him desiring, my waist / old water-moss-like clothes having removed / beautiful flower-like new folded garment having made to wear / joy-giving traditional toddy, not only / nectar-like traditional meat-curry food / in silver and white-metal vessels feeding, not only / in the ancient town's common hall reached, soft-gaited / very large kinsfolk's great suffering to remove / like seeing the blossoms of the kino tree with wet insides / bullock-brought red paddy with stacks having granted / 'may you receive wealth', he said, the drinking ghat / mountain blossoms adorn, the lord of the headwaters land / those who saw, having taken to their house, perfect feet having praised / ... / the sky does not know, my suffering hunger's removal / noble elephant kings / their existence they do not know, seeing they have never known","translation":"Like righteous cowherds raising motherless children with cruel hearts, the cerunti trees bloom with rare flowers in the tall forest, filling the wide courtyard with fragrance like a festival ground. Except for friends who approach, even guards do not enter this protected, wide mansion without permission. Beating my ringing taṭāri drum so that the mountain-like mansion resounded, I stood singing for many days. Not only that, but when I arrived in the anxious night and stood at the tall gate, he said, 'The sparse-haired bard is pitiable,' and desiring to bring me close, he stripped off my old clothes that looked like water-moss, and dressed me in new folded garments like beautiful flowers. He fed me traditional, joy-giving toddy and nectar-like meat curry in silver and white-metal vessels. To remove the great suffering of my soft-gaited, large kinsfolk who had gathered at the common hall of the ancient town, he granted stacks of red paddy brought by bullocks, looking like the wet blossoms of the kino tree, saying, 'May you receive this wealth.' He is the lord of the land of headwaters, where mountain blossoms adorn the drinking ghats. Those who saw us praised his perfect feet... The sky itself does not know how he removed my suffering hunger. Other kings with noble elephants do not even know of his existence, nor have they ever seen him.","modern":"அறநெறி கொண்ட ஆயர்கள் வளர்க்கும் தாய் இல்லாத இரக்கமற்ற குழந்தைகளைப் போல, அரிய மலர்களைக் கொண்ட செருந்தி மரங்கள் அடர்ந்த காட்டில் மலர்ந்து மணம் வீசுகின்றன. விழாக்கோலம் பூண்ட அகன்ற மைதானம் போன்ற அரண்மனை முற்றத்தில், அன்புடையவர்கள் மட்டுமே வர முடியும்; காவலர்கள்கூட அனுமதியின்றி நுழைய முடியாத காவல் மிகுந்த பெரிய மாளிகை அது. மலைக்கூட்டம் போன்ற அந்த மாளிகை அதிருமாறு, எனது ஓசையுடைய தடாரிப் பறையை அடித்துப் பாடிப் பல நாட்கள் நின்றேன். அதுமட்டுமன்றி, ஒரு நாள் கவலையோடு கூடிய இரவில் வந்து அவனது பெரிய வாயிலில் நின்றபோது, 'இந்த வறிய பாணன் இரங்கத்தக்கவன்' என்று கூறி, என்னைத் தன் அருகில் அழைக்க விரும்பினான். பாசி போன்ற எனது பழைய கிழிந்த ஆடைகளைக் களைந்து, மலர் போன்ற புதிய ஆடைகளை உடுத்தச் செய்தான். மகிழ்ச்சி தரும் கள்ளையும், அமிழ்தம் போன்ற இறைச்சி உணவையும் வெள்ளி மற்றும் வெண்கலப் பாத்திரங்களில் ஊட்டி உபசரித்தான். அதுமட்டுமன்றி, அவ்வூர்ப் பொதுச்சாவடியில் தங்கியிருந்த எனது சுற்றத்தாரின் வறுமையைப் போக்க, வேங்கை மலர்களைப் போன்ற செந்நெல் போர்களை வண்டிகளில் ஏற்றித் தந்து, 'இச்செல்வத்தைப் பெற்றுக்கொள்' என்று கூறினான். மலைமலர்கள் மிதந்து வரும் நீர்த்துறையைக் கொண்ட நாட்டின் தலைவன் அவன். அவனைக் கண்டவர்கள் அவனது திருவடிகளை வாழ்த்தினர். எனது பசியைப் போக்கிய அவனது கொடையை வானமும் அறியாது. யானைகளை உடைய பிற வேந்தர்கள் அவனது புகழை அறிய மாட்டார்கள்; அவனைக் கண்டதும் இல்லை.","explanation":"The poet Avvaiyar sings this poem in praise of the chieftain Athiyaman Neduman Anji, belonging to the Paṭāṇ tiṇai. She describes her arrival at his palace in a state of extreme poverty, the warm hospitality she received, and the immense wealth he gifted to her and her kinsfolk. The imagery of the cerunti flowers in the forest, the moss-like old clothes contrasted with flower-like new garments, and the red paddy stacks resembling kino blossoms vividly illustrate the transition from poverty to abundance. The comparison of the chieftain's protective yet welcoming palace to a festive ground highlights his accessibility to friends and poets, while being impenetrable to enemies. Key words like 'அளியன்' (pitiable), 'உடைகளைந்து' (removing clothes), 'புதுமடி' (new garment), and 'செந்நெல்' (red paddy) emphasize the chieftain's deep empathy and boundless generosity.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}